# RegOps frontend environment
#
# Every VITE_-prefixed variable is inlined into the published JavaScript bundle
# and is readable by anyone who loads the page. NEVER put a credential, API key,
# token or signed URL here — the frontend provides no authentication and holds no
# secret. The two variables below are public configuration only.

# VITE_API_MODE selects the adapter returned by src/lib/api/index.ts.
#   mock  (default) — in-memory adapter, full synthetic workflow, no backend needed
#   http            — real HTTP client against the frozen OpenAPI contract
# Anything other than "http" (unset, blank, a typo) falls back to mock, so a
# misconfigured deployment shows obviously synthetic data rather than a
# live-looking console pointed at nothing.
VITE_API_MODE=mock

# Base path for the real HTTP client.
#
# Local default: a relative path. The Vite dev server proxies /api to
# REGOPS_API_PROXY (default http://localhost:8080), so a locally running RegOps
# API needs no CORS entry.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hosted deployment (Vercel) — set these two as build-time Project variables.
# Do not commit them; do not hardcode the host in application code.
#
#   VITE_API_MODE=http
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://regops-api-vx2qltpxca-ey.a.run.app/api/v1
#
# The Cloud Run service must allow the exact hosted HTTPS origin via CORS.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
